      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To gauge environmental risk suggestive of decline, look for demographic shifts like increasing population outflow or an aging customer base in the commercial zones. Economic indicators are key; declining foot traffic counts, rising commercial vacancy rates, and a noticeable slump in local business revenues are strong warning signs. Furthermore, observe changes in local infrastructure maintenance or increased levels of blight, as these signal municipal disinvestment and neighborhood instability. These combined factors help paint a picture of long-term market erosion.",
